// Example URL-loaded customization: studyBrowser/derivedDateTime
//
// Adds the creation date/time to the detail line of every derived series
// thumbnail - SR, SEG, RTSTRUCT, PMAP - in the study browser. Loaded via
// `?customization=studyBrowser/derivedDateTime`.
//
// Derived series are listed newest first, and the date/time they are sorted by
// is the creation date/time of the instance each display set shows (see
// `getSeriesDateTime`). The default thumbnail shows only the series number and
// the instance count, so several reports saved on the same day give no sign of
// which is which and their order reads as arbitrary. This shows it.
//
// Declared the same way as the veterinary demographics overlay
// (`?customization=veterinary/veterinaryOverlay`): a `global` payload naming a
// customization and, for each item, where to get its value from and whether to
// include it. Both are names here rather than functions, so the whole thing is
// data - `source` names a `studyBrowser.thumbnailDetailSources` entry and
// `condition` a `studyBrowser.thumbnailDetailTests` one. Items declared in code
// may pass a `contentF` / `condition` function instead.
//
// `$push` appends to the default items rather than replacing them, so the series
// number and instance count are kept. Use `$set` to replace the whole line.
{
  "global": {
    "studyBrowser.thumbnailDetails": {
      "$push": [
        {
          "id": "InstanceDateTime",
          "source": "instanceDateTime",
          "condition": "isDerivedDisplaySet",
          "title": "Created"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
